# See https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormatStyleOptions.html
#
# Needs clang-format 21, and says so in a way that cannot be missed:
# 'BinPackParameters: OnePerLine' and 'ReflowComments: Always' are spellings
# only 21 accepts, so an older binary refuses the file and formats nothing.
# That refusal is the point. Both options have an older spelling of the same
# meaning, but taking it would let version 19 read the file and then produce a
# different result on many files - it indents neither the include guard nor
# the body of a function-like macro the way 21 does. A loud refusal costs one
# puzzled minute; a silent divergence costs a spurious diff on every review.
#
# The ACT C style, plus the deviations below. Every one of them was found by
# running the formatter over ACT C sources, not chosen a priori:
#
#   AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Empty
#       An empty body is the one block worth keeping on a single line: a
#       deliberate 'for (;;) {}' reads as 'nothing left to do', where the same
#       thing spread over three lines reads as an unfinished edit. Anything
#       with a statement in it still breaks out.
#
#   BraceWrapping: AfterCaseLabel, SplitEmptyFunction
#       A case label that opens a scope only does so to declare something, and
#       the brace belongs on the label rather than a line of its own; an empty
#       function body, like an empty block above, says more collapsed than
#       spread out. Everything else follows the shared style.
#
#   CommentPragmas
#       Reflowing splits a copyright tag that does not fit the column limit
#       across two lines, and the REUSE parser reads only the first: the
#       address ends up on a continuation line that carries no tag and is
#       dropped from the SBOM, while 'reuse lint' still passes, so nothing
#       catches it. The pattern keeps the tool's own default alongside.
#
#   Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
#       Microsoft style breaks a nested designated initialiser onto its own
#       line after the '=', which turns a table of aggregates into one field
#       per two lines and an ever growing indent. This is not cosmetic: such a
#       table is often what a generator has to emit and a reviewer has to
#       read.
#
#   QualifierAlignment: Leave
#       'Left' moves a const in front of the macro that introduces the
#       declaration, so an inline accessor returning a pointer to const comes
#       back as 'const ALWAYS_INLINE uart_t *' - a const sitting in front of
#       the attribute rather than the type. The option is documented as
#       unreliable without full semantic information, and a macro carrying
#       declaration specifiers is exactly what it cannot resolve.
#
#   ReflowComments: Always
#       Frozen comments at this column limit leave prose wider than the code
#       around it, and nothing reports it. Rewrapping keeps the two in step,
#       and CommentPragmas covers the one construct that must not move.

---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Microsoft

AccessModifierOffset: 0
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AlignConsecutiveAssignments: true
AlignConsecutiveMacros: true
AlignEscapedNewlines: Right
AlignOperands: true
AlignTrailingComments: true
AllowAllArgumentsOnNextLine: false
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Empty
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Empty
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
AlwaysBreakAfterDefinitionReturnType: None
AlwaysBreakAfterReturnType: None
AlwaysBreakBeforeMultilineStrings: false
BinPackArguments: false
BinPackParameters: OnePerLine
BraceWrapping:
  AfterCaseLabel: false
  AfterEnum: true
  AfterExternBlock: true
  AfterFunction: true
  AfterStruct: true
  AfterUnion: true
  BeforeElse: true
  SplitEmptyFunction: false
BreakBeforeBinaryOperators: None
BreakBeforeBraces: Custom
BreakStringLiterals: true
ColumnLimit: 80
CommentPragmas: "^ ?(SPDX-|IWYU pragma:)"
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
DerivePointerAlignment: false
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
IndentCaseLabels: true
IndentPPDirectives: AfterHash
IndentWidth: 4
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: false
LineEnding: LF
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 1
PointerAlignment: Right
QualifierAlignment: Leave
ReferenceAlignment: Right
ReflowComments: Always
SortIncludes: true
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: false
SpaceAfterLogicalNot: false
SpaceBeforeAssignmentOperators: true
SpaceBeforeCpp11BracedList: true
SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements
SpaceBeforeRangeBasedForLoopColon: false
SpaceInEmptyBlock: false
SpaceInEmptyParentheses: false
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 1
SpacesInAngles: false
SpacesInContainerLiterals: false
SpacesInCStyleCastParentheses: false
SpacesInParentheses: false
SpacesInSquareBrackets: false
Standard: Auto
...
